# Replacements for the shader inspector

*plugin* `shader-inspector`

All hooks call `self.dsm_shader?.…`. The shared module is also evaluated on
the main thread, where `dsm_shader` is not defined, so the hooks are no-ops
there.

## Track which expression each parse node belongs to

*Description* `Track the expression being compiled, for the shader inspector`

*worker_only*

The node compiler is wrapped instead of edited inside, so the tracking is
undone even when compiling throws.

*Find* => `from`
```js
function $tt($e, $t) {
  let { chunk: $r } = $e, $n;
  $Fk();
  let $o = $iae($e, $t);
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
function $tt($e, $t) {
  const __dsmPrev = self.dsm_shader?.enter($t);
  try {
    return __dsmShaderCompileNode($e, $t);
  } finally {
    self.dsm_shader?.exit(__dsmPrev);
  }
}
function __dsmShaderCompileNode($e, $t) {
  let { chunk: $r } = $e, $n;
  $Fk();
  let $o = $iae($e, $t);
```

## Tag each instruction with its expression

*Description* `Tag compiler instructions with their expression, for the shader inspector`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
pushInstructionChecked($t) {
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
pushInstructionChecked($t) {
  self.dsm_shader?.tag(this, $t);
```

## Remember the expression of each constant the GLSL emitter prints

*Description* `Track which expression each shader uniform comes from`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
emitConstant($r) {
  return this.printValue($r, $r.mobility)
}
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
emitConstant($r) {
  self.dsm_shader?.constant(this, $r);
  return this.printValue($r, $r.mobility)
}
```

## Record the expression of each shader uniform

*Description* `Record which expression each shader uniform comes from`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
let $i = "_DCG_SC_" + this.shaderUniforms.length;
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
self.dsm_shader?.uniform(this);
let $i = "_DCG_SC_" + this.shaderUniforms.length;
```

## Record the expression of each shader list

*Description* `Record which expression each shader list comes from`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
return this.listConstants.push($f), $p
}
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
return self.dsm_shader?.list(this), this.listConstants.push($f), $p
}
```

## Attach the expressions behind a shader to it

*Description* `Attach per-expression shader details for the shader inspector`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
costEstimate: $qd(this.chunk),
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
costEstimate: self.dsm_shader
  ? self.dsm_shader.cost(this, () => $qd(this.chunk))
  : $qd(this.chunk),
dsmInfo: self.dsm_shader?.report(this),
```

## Attribute each instruction's cost estimate to its expression

*Description* `Attribute shader cost estimates to expressions`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
$Po($a) ? ($i += $joe($e, $s, $a, $n), $s = $a.endIndex) : $i += $Joe($e, $s, $n)
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
$Po($a)
  ? ($i += $joe($e, $s, $a, $n), $s = $a.endIndex)
  : $i += self.dsm_shader
      ? self.dsm_shader.leaf($e, $s, $Joe($e, $s, $n))
      : $Joe($e, $s, $n)
```

## Record each sum and product in a shader's cost estimate

*Description* `Record shader sums and products and their cost`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
Math.round($w($q.value)));
if (!isFinite($s)) return 1 / 0;
if ($s === 0) return 0;
let $a = $SF($e, $t + 1, $r.endIndex - 1, $n);
return $s * $a
}
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
Math.round($w($q.value)));
if (!isFinite($s)) return 1 / 0;
if ($s === 0) return 0;
let $a = self.dsm_shader
  ? self.dsm_shader.loop($e, $r, $s, () => $SF($e, $t + 1, $r.endIndex - 1, $n))
  : $SF($e, $t + 1, $r.endIndex - 1, $n);
return $s * $a
}
```

## Record each list operation in a shader's cost estimate

*Description* `Record shader list operations and their cost`

*worker_only*

*Find* => `from`
```js
let $i = $v($o.value);
if (!isFinite($i)) return 1 / 0;
if ($i === 0) return 0;
let $s = $SF($e, $t + 1, $r.endIndex - 1, $n);
return $i * $s
}
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
let $i = $v($o.value);
if (!isFinite($i)) return 1 / 0;
if ($i === 0) return 0;
let $s = self.dsm_shader
  ? self.dsm_shader.loop($e, $r, $i, () => $SF($e, $t + 1, $r.endIndex - 1, $n))
  : $SF($e, $t + 1, $r.endIndex - 1, $n);
return $i * $s
}
```

## Keep an instruction's expression when the compiler copies it

*Description* `Keep the expression of copied compiler instructions`

*worker_only*

Broadcasting and other transforms rebuild instructions while compiling some
other node. The copy belongs to the original's expression.

*Find* => `from`
```js
function $Yh($e, $t, $r) {
  switch ($t.type) {
    case 8:
      return $e.Add($r);
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
function $Yh($e, $t, $r) {
  const __dsmPrev = self.dsm_shader?.copying($t);
  try {
    return __dsmShaderCopyInstruction($e, $t, $r);
  } finally {
    self.dsm_shader?.copied(__dsmPrev);
  }
}
function __dsmShaderCopyInstruction($e, $t, $r) {
  switch ($t.type) {
    case 8:
      return $e.Add($r);
```

## Give a folded constant the expression of the value it came from

*Description* `Keep the expression of constant-folded values`

*worker_only*

Folding pops the instruction and pushes its value as a constant. The value
comes from the arguments, so it belongs to whichever of them can change.

*Find* => `from`
```js
popInstruction() {
  this.unsafelyTruncate(this.instructions.length - 1)
}
```

*Replace* `from` with
```js
popInstruction() {
  self.dsm_shader?.popped(this);
  this.unsafelyTruncate(this.instructions.length - 1)
}
```
